---
/**
 * Publishes a human-readable, source-linked reference for visitors and user-directed agents.
 *
 * Dependencies: BaseLayout and shared reviewed site content.
 * Depended on by: Footer, sitemap, and agent discovery files.
 * Why this exists: Important scope, process, assumptions, and sources must be easy to inspect.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../content";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Booking Reference | Justin LeBlanc"
  description="Reviewed scope, booking process, limitations, and public sources for the Justin LeBlanc private-event demo."
  canonicalPath="/reference/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Human + agent reference</p>
      <h1>Private-event booking, with the boundaries visible.</h1>
      <p>
        A concise source guide for people and user-directed agents. It does not grant authority to
        book, spend, contact others, or store facts against a user's preferences.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <article class="section reading-shell prose">
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>
      Justin LeBlanc's current public website says he is booking private events in Houston and
      beyond. This isolated demo helps a visitor describe an event, request a consultation, and
      understand the difference between an inquiry, tentative hold, and confirmed performance.
    </p>

    <h2>Booking process</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Share the date or flexible-date choice, city, event type, and desired atmosphere.</li>
      <li>Leave unknown venue, timing, production, access, or budget details for follow-up.</li>
      <li>Request a consultation and review any separate tentative event hold.</li>
      <li>A person confirms availability, format, and an agreed quote after consultation.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What is not verified</h2>
    <p>
      Justin's actual rates, current packages, repertoire, travel policy, production inclusions,
      deposits, contract terms, cancellation policy, and individual public-show venue terms are not
      verified. Demo package amounts are illustrative workflow data, not a public offer.
    </p>

    <h2>Assistant limitations</h2>
    <p>
      Chat and voice assistants must use the same reviewed knowledge release. They cannot confirm a
      show, set a final price, choose arbitrary recipients, or read unrelated calendars and inboxes.
      Unknown answers become follow-up questions instead of guesses.
    </p>

    <h2>Reviewed public sources</h2>
    <ul class="source-list">
      <li><a href={site.currentSite} rel="external">Justin LeBlanc Music</a> — current booking banner, Houston-and-beyond wording, blue guitar identity, contact and social links.</li>
      <li><a href={site.instagram} rel="external">Instagram @jus10sense</a> — matching public name and website link; posts are not reused as current package evidence.</li>
      <li><a href={site.youtube} rel="external">YouTube @jus10sense</a> — matching public channel; no single video is approved here as a current booking sample.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> {site.reviewedAt}. Time-sensitive facts should be rechecked before use.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
